00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:55.900
the anchors have been
asking me the same question.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:57.930
What's the deal with community spread?

00:10:57.930 --> 00:11:00.189
Because there was a
single case in California,

00:11:00.189 --> 00:11:03.040
where we had an individual
who tested positive

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:06.410
for the coronavirus,
without exposure to someone

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:09.100
from an area where the
coronavirus is present,

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:11.030
or someone actively sick.

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:13.393
In those situations we
label that community spread.

00:11:13.393 --> 00:11:16.120
In this situation
research is still ongoing,

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:18.130
to figure out how that person was sick,

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:20.630
so we're not labeling it
community spread just yet,

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:22.670
we're suspecting that
it's community spread.

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:25.250
I'll give you an example, if
a patient comes into my office

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:27.666
with the influenza virus,
and I diagnose them

00:11:27.666 --> 00:11:30.790
with the influenza virus, I
don't go and do an investigation

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.250
of how they got it.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:34.210
I just say hey, you got
it from the community,

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:36.230
so we label it community spread.

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:38.430
If community spread starts happening,

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:40.640
meaning that there's
patients that are coughing

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:42.170
and sneezing walking around

00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:43.670
and they're not being quarantined,

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:45.540
and put into isolation properly,

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:48.240
that can cause a huge uptick in cases.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.660
Something else that could be going on,

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:51.210
which we're just learning about,

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:52.870
is that there's some patients

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:55.730
that are having asymptomatic
spread of this virus.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:57.760
Meaning that they're not showing symptoms,

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:00.260
the virus is in an incubation stage,

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:03.310
which we're saying lasts
anywhere from two to 14 days,

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:05.750
huge range, at which time where,

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:07.620
they could possibly spread the virus,

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:09.060
but not show any symptoms.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:12.060
That could be problematic on
one hand, but also positive

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.680
on another, meaning that there's a lot

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:15.520
of cases we haven't diagnosed yet,

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:17.890
which will lower the
lethality rate of the virus,

00:12:17.890 --> 00:12:19.630
making it less dangerous.

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.870
So we have to figure it
out, we have to wait,

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:25.230
and we have to not rush to look
at numbers every single day.

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:26.670
Those numbers will change,

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:28.737
those numbers will grow
one day, shrink another.

00:12:28.737 --> 00:12:32.120
Let's look at averages,
let's look at guidance

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:35.110
from trustworthy sources,
like the CDC, and WHO,

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:35.970
and go from there.

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:38.570
Check out my video of
me playing Plague Inc.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.870
Now you may laugh, why
am I recommending a game

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:42.690
where you're infecting the world,

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.660
but it actually teaches
you a lot of lessons

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.530
about how viruses like this spread.

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:49.092
Definitely give it a click
and stay happy and healthy.

00:12:49.092 --> 00:12:51.759
(upbeat music)

